# ---- Large numbers and the curves P-256, P-384 and P-521 ----
# A number is limbs of 64 bits, the lowest first, at an address; the
# runtime multiplies them (spec/tls-x86_64.s). A text of zero bytes for k
# limbs, and its address.
#: _lz/1
  def _lz(k: integer): integer do
    Sys.addr(String.duplicate("\x00", 8 * k + 8))
  end
# The limbs, k of them at a new address, of the number a text writes with
# its highest byte first.
